    "response": "open the circuit so that further executions on that connection fail immediately, without attempting the command, for the connection's configured circuit-breaker test interval",
    "subject": "Resilient Command Execution",
    "trigger": "consecutive execution failures on that connection reach the configured circuit-breaker failure count (where transient database errors are filtered and retried via services.GetIsErrorTransient(ex) before an unrecovered failure counts toward the circuit-breaker threshold)",
    "where": "the connection's CircuitBreakerFailureCount is left unconfigured (null) or is explicitly configured to 1 or more"
  },
